    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d319">

                <pb facs="0360" n="286" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v01/pg286"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/7545</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rome</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-11-02T13:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 2, 1917, 1 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received November 3, 9.10
                        a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1171. Situation unchanged, only more news coming of Second Army’s going on strike
                    and declaring for peace with exception of certain units that fought till
                    extirpated. All depends whether the <pb facs="0361" n="287" xml:id="pg287"/>
                    insidious propaganda based on socialists’ literature and the Pope’s peace
                    suggestions have undermined other forces, especially Third Army on which rest
                    hopes of immediate defense and time for reorganization. If Italy can reorganize
                    promptly Second Army, the disaster not irremediable because the Allies are
                    rushing in troops. At present Italians reported holding part of the Tagliamento
                    line though believe that they are falling back on Piave line. British and French
                    will require perhaps fortnight to get in action in force. British Chief of Staff
                        Robertson and General Foch are here to-day canvassing
                    situation. Intention is to try for the present to hold Venice; all depends on
                    Italy’s power to keep up fight. Little information given out but people so far
                    calm and firm.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nelson Page</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
